<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        ellekit filter plist for VcamFullMay.

        Live testing on Dopamine 2 / ellekit 1.1.3 confirmed: `Filter > Bundles`
        only matches FRAMEWORK bundle IDs in a process's dyld-loaded bundle
        list (com.apple.UIKit, com.apple.Foundation, …). It does NOT match
        the app's own CFBundleIdentifier (vn.com.vng.zingalo etc.) regardless
        of `Mode=Any`. Listing app IDs never caused injection into Zalo on
        this device.

        To actually reach Zalo / Facebook / etc., we filter on UIKit
        (loaded by every UI app, including system processes). Safety is
        provided by:
          1. vcam_unsafe_host() in %ctor — bails on sh/bash/sudo/sshd/...
          2. vcam_target_app() in %ctor — bails on non-target bundle IDs
          3. g_vcam_active flag — every %hook method falls through to %orig
             when the flag is unset, so even the +load-installed swizzles
             are no-ops in non-target processes.

        Result: dylib loads into many processes (cheap — just ROM-mapped),
        %ctor returns early in non-target apps, hooks stay inert. Only
        bundle IDs in vcam_target_app's allowlist get hooks active.
    -->
    <key>Filter</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Bundles</key>
        <array>
            <string>com.apple.UIKit</string>
        </array>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
